\begin_layout Section
Models
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In what follows,
 we develop our spatially-resolved SPMe for LIB half cells.
 As the SPMe+ combines elements from the perturbation model and a vanilla SPMe,
 we review those models first.
 In addition,
 we review the full-order PDAE model against which we validate the SPMe+.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Full-Order PDAE Model
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We employ a PDAE model based on the Doyle–Fuller–Newman pseudo-two-dimensional model 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "DFN1993"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 to validate our proposed model.
 As discussed by ref.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "hileman2024physics"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 we incorporate several improvements,
 including:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Lumping the standard intensive parameters into a number of extensive parameters,
 all of which may be estimated without ambiguity from cell-level voltage,
 current and temperature measurements.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Adding a description of the electrical double-layer.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Using the Multi-Site Multi-Reaction (MSMR) open-circuit potential (OCP) and intercalation reaction kinetics model given by Verbrugge et al.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "VerbruggeMSMR"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Using the concentration-dependent solid diffusion model specified by Baker and Verbrugge
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "BakerVerbruggeDiff"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Fig.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:HC-cross-section"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

 illustrates the regions of an LIB half-cell in the PDAE model:
 dead-lithium layer (dll),
 separator (sep),
 and porous positive electrode (pos) with respective thicknesses 
\begin_inset Formula $L^{\mathrm{d}}$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $L^{\mathrm{s}}$
\end_inset

,
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $L^{\mathrm{p}}$
\end_inset

.
 Dimensionless position along the sandwich is 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{x}$
\end_inset

 and dimensionless radial position within spherical particles is 
\begin_inset Formula $\tilde{r}$
\end_inset

.
 As discussed in ref.
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
